    "role": "caster",
    "tier": 2,
    "factionId": "",
    "notes": "<p>A walking argument: unnaturally tall and thin, skin a bruised patchwork of clashing colors, head featureless except for a single oversized, sneering mouth that never stops moving. Drawn to peace like flies to sugar — negotiations, gatherings, quiet libraries — where its whispers exploit every insecurity until civil discussion becomes bloodshed. It doesn't need to win fights. Only to start them.</p><p><strong>Qliphah:</strong> Thagirion, the Conflicts — the Hull of Tiferet. Harmony shattered into endless, ugly strife.</p><p><em>Mal's note: 'If everyone at the table is suddenly RIGHT and FURIOUS about it, someone let a Disputant in the door.'</em></p>",
